WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.650
More than a century ago, a boy named Shlomo Keha
grew up in the mountains of northern Yemen.

2
00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:14.000
As a boy, he shared a book with three other
children. Years later in Aden, his own pupils
would sit around him.

3
00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:18.800
There was a long road between those two
schoolrooms. This is how Shlomo remembered it.

4
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:22.820
In the study house in northern Yemen, books were
scarce.

5
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:26.420
“There were four of us children to one book.”

6
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.960
Each child read from the side where he sat.

7
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:32.560
Shlomo was very small when he lost his father.

8
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:38.015
“When my mother died, I was perhaps fifteen.”

9
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:41.620
With both parents gone, Shlomo went to live with
his father’s sister, Badra.

10
00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:44.910
At nineteen, as he remembered it, he left the
mountains.

11
00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:50.550
Shlomo turned south. The port of Aden was still
days away on foot.

12
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:56.100
Pack donkeys made their way alongside the
travelers.

13
00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:04.830
“From place to place. We walked by day and slept
at night.”

14
00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:10.300
In Aden, the boy who had shared a book now had
pupils of his own.

15
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:13.970
“I had children there, and I taught them.”

16
00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:20.960
Aden granted the permit. He recalled being twenty
and giving his age as twenty-five.

17
00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:24.430
After about a year of teaching and waiting, it
was time to sail.

18
00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.790
“From Aden we went by ship.”

19
00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:35.250
Until now the journey was measured in footsteps.
From here the sea would carry him.

20
00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:41.650
The ship sailed north through the Red Sea to the
Suez Canal.

21
00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.890
“We stayed in Port Said for one day.”

22
00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:52.970
Beyond the canal, the journey changed again. This
time there were wheels.

23
00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:59.910
“Then they sent a vehicle for us from the Land of
Israel.”

24
00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.940
In Tel Aviv, Shlomo stayed at the immigrants’
hostel.

25
00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:07.540
In 1938, Shlomo married Yona Nakash.

26
00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:10.850
Four years later, here they are together in the
family album.
